{"record":"parent_entry","position":{"parent_record":"request:00000000000000000046:0000","subposition":null},"original_role":"tool","source":"tool_result","trust":"untrusted","provenance":null,"content":"{\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"call_id\":\"call_01a169ffbc2d7504ba7682c5399f9780\",\"output\":\"Read text file `Blog, CMS & Community Platforms/Forumino/README.md`.\\n1|# Forum Implementation\\n2|  \\n3|This is a project built with [Chef](https://chef.convex.dev) using [Convex](https://convex.dev) as its backend.\\n4|  \\n5|This project is connected to the Convex deployment named [`patient-rat-995`](https://dashboard.convex.dev/d/patient-rat-995).\\n6|  \\n7|## Project structure\\n8|  \\n9|The frontend code is in the `app` directory and is built with [Vite](https://vitejs.dev/).\\n10|  \\n11|The backend code is in the `convex` directory.\\n12|  \\n13|`npm run dev` will start the frontend and backend servers.\\n14|\\n15|## App authentication\\n16|\\n17|Chef apps use [Convex Auth](https://auth.convex.dev/) with Anonymous auth for easy sign in. You may wish to change this before deploying your app.\\n18|\\n19|## Developing and deploying your app\\n20|\\n21|Check out the [Convex docs](https://docs.convex.dev/) for more information on how to develop with Convex.\\n22|* If you're new to Convex, the [Overview](https://docs.convex.dev/understanding/) is a good place to start\\n23|* Check out the [Hosting and Deployment](https://docs.convex.dev/production/) docs for how to deploy your app\\n24|* Read the [Best Practices](https://docs.convex.dev/understanding/best-practices/) guide for tips on how to improve you app further\"}","truncated":false}
{"record":"parent_entry","position":{"parent_record":"request:00000000000000000047:0000","subposition":null},"original_role":"tool","source":"tool_result","trust":"untrusted","provenance":null,"content":"{\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"call_id\":\"call_01a169ffbdf2739d91f9d72c80cf9c74\",\"output\":\"Read text file `Blog, CMS & Community Platforms/BlogForge/README.md`.\\n1|# BlogForge\\n2|\\n3|A modern blog/CMS system built with Flask and MariaDB.\\n4|\\n5|## Features\\n6|\\n7|- User authentication and registration\\n8|- Admin dashboard for content management\\n9|- Markdown support for blog posts\\n10|- Image upload support\\n11|- Responsive design using Bootstrap\\n12|- SEO-friendly URLs\\n13|\\n14|## Prerequisites\\n15|\\n16|- Python 3.8+\\n17|- MariaDB 10.5+\\n18|- NGINX (for production)\\n19|- Python virtual environment\\n20|\\n21|## Local Development Setup\\n22|\\n23|1. Create a virtual environment and activate it:\\n24|   ```bash\\n25|   python -m venv venv\\n26|   # On Windows:\\n27|   venv\\\\Scripts\\\\activate\\n28|   # On Linux/Mac:\\n29|   source venv/bin/activate\\n30|   ```\\n31|\\n32|2. Install required packages:\\n33|   ```bash\\n34|   pip install -r requirements.txt\\n35|   ```\\n36|\\n37|3. Configure MariaDB:\\n38|   ```sql\\n39|   CREATE DATABASE blogforge CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;\\n40|   CREATE USER 'blogforge'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'your_password';\\n41|   GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON blogforge.* TO 'blogforge'@'localhost';\\n42|   FLUSH PRIVILEGES;\\n43|   ```\\n44|\\n45|4. Set up environment variables by copying `.env.example` to `.env` and updating the values:\\n46|   ```\\n47|   FLASK_APP=app\\n48|   FLASK_ENV=development\\n49|   SECRET_KEY=your-super-secret-key\\n50|   DB_HOST=localhost\\n51|   DB_USER=blogforge\\n52|   DB_PASSWORD=your_password\\n53|   DB_NAME=blogforge\\n54|   ```\\n55|\\n56|5. Initialize the database:\\n57|   ```bash\\n58|   flask db upgrade\\n59|   ```\\n60|\\n(more lines below)\"}","truncated":false}
